==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Kenshin Himura CC''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Wanderer Who Does Not Kill・Kenshin Himura''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Kenshin Himura can be comparable to [[Kung Fu Cat (Special Cat)|Dancer Cat's]] [[Dancer Cat (Enemy)|enemy counterpart]], as his high range is useful against most enemies, even the ones [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] struggles against, such as [[Master A.]] and [[THE SLOTH]]. His Surge Immunity and massive damage make him an excellent counter against [[Kappy Jr.]] and [[Kappy Kawano]] as well. Against [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] enemies however, his role falls off against [[Fallen Bear]], [[Le'Behemoth]], and [[Vermilingua Rangmaster|Rangmaster]], because it's difficult for him to get attacks off when their shields are active, and because of a lack of [[:Category:Shield Piercing Cats|Shield Piercing]]. He can be used in [[Surge Attack|Surge]]-heavy stages, since he can't be harmed by [[:Category:Death Surge Enemies|Death Surge]] enemies, or just Surge enemies in general, such as [[Red EnerG]].

==='''True Form'''===

Despite Wanderer Who Does Not Kill・Kenshin Himura's lower DPS and attack frequency, he's an unbelievable improvement over his Evolved Form in almost every aspect. For starters, the pierce on his Long Distance attacks is absolutely gargantuan, hitting all the way up to 800 range—an additional 365 range past his standing range. Though this comes at the cost of a blind spot, it is virtually non-existent for all intents and purposes, as a majority of targets are simply not capable of pushing hard enough to infiltrate without getting juggled to death by Kenshin in the process. Furthermore, he loses the attack cooldown and becomes a rebound attacker, which works to his benefit as an improvement to survivability, now retaliating instantly on enemies who deal enough damage to stagger him.

His DPH is improved slightly from his Evolved Form to compensate the hit on his attack cooldown, which only complements his role as a nuker. On average, he deals 124,950 DPH against targets at Lv.30, which translates to 14,994 DPS (198,450 DPH and 23,814 at Lv.50); impressive numbers for a unit with as much area coverage as he does. Many previously mediocre matchups into enemies like [[Mr. Mole]], Master A., [[Dolphina]], [[Camelle]], [[Rain D.]], and even [[Poultrio]], are massively improved to such a degree that he is now a top tier nuker within his niches. Additionally, [[Special Abilities#Immune to Freeze|Freeze Immunity]] makes him a [[Henry]] counter as the cherry on top.

